{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to question c3f2f50d (R7 hardening preparation, 5e6d482c).\n\n1. Versions. Agreed: Rules 11 and Destination 14 have shipped (they are\n   on Main and served by VERSIONS), so their data and rules do not change.\n   The hardening head creates the next versions. Reserved: Destination 15\n   for the one-use certificate marker, the record ceiling and the\n   liveness answer. Bump Register, Directory or Rules only if their data\n   or rules change (for example, if the family or the creating definition\n   names the destination version); say which and why in the note. Keep\n   Q11, G14, R19 and D18 exact.\n   Order, reconciled: the hardening head is the next platform version\n   after R7 and goes before BR-13. BR-13 (487496f5) now reads \"after the\n   archive milestone; before the next platform version after the R7\n   hardening\". Reason: the hardening is small and security-owned, and the\n   certified cohort should not be enabled with known limits; BR-13's\n   golden table is generated from the lists as they stand when it starts,\n   so the new versions only add rows.\n\n2. Liveness. A named native certificate-declined answer that carries the\n   immutable intervening fact (started.seq+1, or the entry observed after\n   the held read) satisfies item 2 of 5e6d482c. The request asks for a\n   deterministic answer naming the intervening entry instead of silence;\n   a declined outcome with that fact is deterministic and lets the member\n   decide to retry. Refuse before I/O or after the held I/O where the host\n   can; decline with the fact in the final race between host return and\n   outcome recording. No outcome-normalization contract and no kernel\n   change for this head; if you believe one is needed, file it as a\n   separate design question under the coherence filing gate.\n\n3. Other choices, accepted as proposed: one-use publication through the\n   existing certificate.request monotone marker (same full Destination\n   ref, strictly greater request seq, committed with the publication; no\n   scan, no new unbounded set, no cross-scope consume); the record ceiling\n   reserves the full entry overhead and the maximal 32 generation proofs\n   before capture, and the witness measures the full stored entry plus\n   record and refuses over-bound before capture; the Page says that no\n   user-facing publish command ships yet.\n\nStill after BR-3 and before the cohort is enabled.","body":{"to":"builder"}}